# Run-time outputs of the L4 end-to-end runs. Each arm writes a full agent
# trajectory tree (per-instance profiles, patches, logs, report.json), which is
# both large and machine-specific: it carries host paths, container ids, the
# proxy port that happened to be free, and the API endpoint in use. This
# workspace keeps its own reports/ so L1, L2, L3 and L4 numbers never mix, and
# nothing report-shaped is committed wherever it lands.
reports/
runs/
*_REPORT.md
*_REPORT_zh.md
*_REPORT_DIFF.md
report.json

# Resolved agent configs. assets/configs/ holds the committed templates, which
# reference credentials through ${DASHSCOPE_API_KEY} interpolation; anything
# rendered locally has the key substituted in and must never be committed.
assets/configs/*.resolved.json

# Proxy logs from the compression arms. These contain per-request
# tokens_before/tokens_after, and with them the payloads' shape and size.
*.proxy.log
__pycache__/

# Run trees recovered from the evaluation hosts: agent profiles, SQLite
# transcripts, tarballs, and per-host environment fingerprints (revisions, pip
# freezes, image digests, working-tree snapshots). All of it is run-specific
# data tied to a particular machine, not part of the harness, so none of it is
# committed to this public repository -- it stays local and is re-derivable from
# the host that produced the numbers.
archive/
